{
  "id": "aio_libs_aiohttp_13302",
  "repo_name": "aio-libs/aiohttp",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp",
  "base_commit": "073ee844bc1dfa30db191118c7f2cf119c96debb",
  "pr_number": 13302,
  "issue_number": 13274,
  "issue_title": "WebSocket regression in 3.14.2: compressed data rejected after initial PONG",
  "issue_body": "### Describe the bug\n\naiohttp 3.14.2/3.14.3 rejects a valid compressed WebSocket data frame when the first inbound frame is a control frame.\n\n  The reproducible sequence is:\n\n  1. An aiohttp server sends PING.\n  2. The client replies with PONG.\n  3. The client sends a compressed TEXT frame using the negotiated permessage-deflate extension.\n  4. The aiohttp server closes with WebSocket protocol error 1002:\n\n     Received frame with non-zero reserved bits\n\n  The same sequence works correctly with aiohttp 3.14.1.\n\n  This appears to be a regression introduced by PR #12988 (\"keep websocket compression state across interleaved control frames\"). PONG followed by compressed application data is a\n  valid WebSocket sequence; control frames may be interleaved with data frames under RFC 6455 \u00a75.4.\n\n\n\n### To Reproduce\n\n```\nimport asyncio\n\n  import aiohttp\n  from aiohttp import WSMsgType, web\n\n\n  async def main() -> None:\n      pong_received = asyncio.Event()\n      server_result = asyncio.get_running_loop().create_future()\n\n      async def websocket_handler(request: web.Request) -> web.WebSocketResponse:\n          # Disable server autoping so the reproducer can observe the PONG.\n          # Compression remains enabled and is negotiated with the client.\n          ws = web.WebSocketResponse(autoping=False, compress=True)\n          await ws.prepare(request)\n\n          await ws.ping()\n          pong = await ws.receive()\n          assert pong.type is WSMsgType.PONG\n          pong_received.set()\n\n          message = await ws.receive()\n          server_result.set_result((message.type, message.data, ws.exception()))\n          await ws.close()\n          return ws\n\n      app = web.Application()\n      app.router.add_get(\"/\", websocket_handler)\n      runner = web.AppRunner(app)\n      await runner.setup()\n\n      site = web.TCPSite(runner, \"127.0.0.1\", 0)\n      await site.start()\n\n      try:\n          async with aiohttp.ClientSession() as session:\n              async with session.ws_connect(\n                  f\"http://127.0.0.1:{site.port}/\",\n                  compress=15,\n              ) as ws:\n                  # receive() processes the server PING, automatically sends\n                  # PONG, and then waits for the server's close frame.\n                  receive_task = asyncio.create_task(ws.receive())\n\n                  await pong_received.wait()\n                  await ws.send_str(\"hello\")\n\n                  message_type, data, exception = await server_result\n                  print(f\"aiohttp {aiohttp.__version__}\")\n                  print(f\"server message type: {message_type.name}\")\n                  print(f\"server message data: {data!r}\")\n                  print(f\"server exception: {exception!r}\")\n\n                  await receive_task\n      finally:\n          await runner.cleanup()\n\n\n  asyncio.run(main())\n\n\n```  Run with:\n\n  $ python -m pip install aiohttp==3.14.3\n  $ python repro.py\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe server should accept and decompress the TEXT message after receiving PONG.\n\n  Expected output, as produced by aiohttp 3.14.1:\n\n  aiohttp 3.14.1\n  server message type: TEXT\n  server message data: 'hello'\n  server exception: None\n\n\n\n### Logs/tracebacks\n\n```python-traceback\naiohttp 3.14.3\n  server message type: ERROR\n  server message data: WebSocketError(<WSCloseCode.PROTOCOL_ERROR: 1002>, 'Received frame with non-zero reserved bits')\n  server exception: WebSocketError(<WSCloseCode.PROTOCOL_ERROR: 1002>, 'Received frame with non-zero reserved bits')\n```\n\n### Python Version\n\n```console\n$ python --version\n  Python 3.14.1\n```\n\n### aiohttp Version\n\n```console\n$ python -m pip show aiohttp\nVersion: 3.14.3\n```\n\n### multidict Version\n\n```console\n$ python -m pip show multidict\nVersion: 6.6.4\n```\n\n### propcache Version\n\n```console\n$ python -m pip show propcache\nVersion: 0.3.2\n```\n\n### yarl Version\n\n```console\n$ python -m pip show yarl\nVersion: 1.20.1\n```\n\n### OS\n\nUbuntu 26.04 LTS, Linux x86_64, glibc 2.43\n\n\n### Related component\n\nServer\n\n### Additional context\n\nSuspected cause:\n\n  PR #12988 changed `_frame_fin` so that only data frames update it, preserving the compression state when a control frame occurs inside a fragmented message.\n\n  However, compression-state selection still occurs before that condition. If PONG is the first inbound frame:\n\n  - `_compressed` is set to COMPRESSED_FALSE from the control frame.\n  - `_frame_fin` remains false because the frame is a control frame.\n  - The next compressed data frame has RSV1 set.\n  - Since `_frame_fin` is false and `_compressed` is no longer COMPRESSED_NOT_SET, the parser rejects RSV1 with protocol error 1002.\n\n  The regression is also reproducible with a Chromium browser connecting to an aiohttp server. Pinning aiohttp to 3.14.1 resolves it.\n\n  Relevant links:\n\n  - https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/pull/12988\n  - https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6455.html#section-5.4\n\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [x] I agree to follow the aio-libs Code of Conduct",
